WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.379
The cost of government failure.

00:00:02.329 --> 00:00:05.056
One hundred and three billion dollars.

00:00:05.056 --> 00:00:14.068
That is the running total of documented government financial failures sourced exclusively from Auditor General reports, the Parliamentary Budget Officer, and Health Canada data.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:17.931
Every dollar on this page comes from the government's own records.

00:00:17.931 --> 00:00:21.511
This is what institutional failure costs Canadians.

00:00:21.511 --> 00:00:22.920
The ledger.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.556
Thirty-two billion in unverified pandemic benefits.

00:00:26.556 --> 00:00:30.011
Nine point three billion for the Phoenix Pay disaster.

00:00:30.011 --> 00:00:33.772
Two point two billion in ArriveCAN and procurement waste.

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:37.943
One point five eight billion in palliative care avoided through MAID.

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:41.431
Seventy-eight point three billion in projected deficit.

00:00:41.431 --> 00:00:44.602
Every line item from official government reports.

00:00:44.602 --> 00:00:46.431
Per capita cost.

00:00:46.431 --> 00:00:53.818
One hundred and three billion dollars divided by forty-one million Canadians equals approximately twenty-five hundred dollars per person.

00:00:53.818 --> 00:01:00.318
Every man, woman, and child in Canada has paid twenty-five hundred dollars for the government's documented failures.

00:01:00.318 --> 00:01:03.443
A family of four: ten thousand dollars.

00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:05.613
This is not theoretical.

00:01:05.613 --> 00:01:08.249
These are the government's own numbers.
